WEBVTT

00:49.321 --> 00:52.071
He put up a valiant fight

00:52.151 --> 00:54.531
against a group of English soldiers.

00:55.571 --> 00:58.321
But he was stabbed from behind with a spear,
and tragically...

00:59.161 --> 01:02.161
Please accept my sincere condolences,
Your Highness.

01:06.371 --> 01:09.501
We were eating rabbit stew,

01:09.591 --> 01:11.551
and then he left suddenly.

01:16.841 --> 01:18.141
That's weird.

01:18.221 --> 01:19.471
Just now...

01:20.511 --> 01:21.601
But...

01:26.021 --> 01:27.771
We shall leave immediately.

01:27.851 --> 01:28.851
Get ready.

01:29.521 --> 01:30.441
Thorfinn.

01:30.521 --> 01:32.401
Don't leave him alone.

01:32.481 --> 01:36.741
What? You're kidding me! I don't want to!

01:36.821 --> 01:38.111
Hey! Wait!

01:38.201 --> 01:40.991
Guarding the prince is your job!

01:41.081 --> 01:42.281
No!

03:17.591 --> 03:19.761
He's paralyzed with fear.

03:19.841 --> 03:22.471
Is that weakling of a prince going to be okay?

03:22.931 --> 03:25.261
I think your plan backfired, Askeladd.

03:25.351 --> 03:27.011
Maybe you shouldn't have killed Ragnar.

03:27.101 --> 03:28.431
HISTORY OF BEASTS

03:28.521 --> 03:30.141
Don't talk so loudly.

03:30.771 --> 03:33.441
Most of the men don't know what really happened.

03:33.521 --> 03:36.441
The English are the ones who did it.

03:36.521 --> 03:37.651
Don't let the secret out.

03:37.731 --> 03:39.901
I wonder...

03:39.991 --> 03:43.031
Everyone knows you didn't get along with Ragnar.

03:43.111 --> 03:45.531
He may be weak, but he's going to realize
what happened.

03:45.621 --> 03:48.411
As long as there's no proof, it will be fine.

03:48.491 --> 03:50.121
The reason the prince is so weak

03:50.201 --> 03:52.411
is because Ragnar spoiled him.

03:52.501 --> 03:54.581
I had to make Ragnar disappear.

03:54.671 --> 03:56.291
Otherwise, he'd cause me grief.

03:56.381 --> 03:58.551
The fact that he's weak is a good thing.

03:58.631 --> 04:00.171
It makes him easy to control.

04:00.261 --> 04:03.551
He can be used as the perfect stepping stone
to achieve greatness in the world.

04:07.851 --> 04:08.721
Bjorn.

04:09.891 --> 04:12.851
Why have you served me for all this time?

04:14.271 --> 04:16.901
Well, it's...

04:16.981 --> 04:18.981
because I wanted to.

04:19.691 --> 04:20.861
I'm the same.

04:21.861 --> 04:24.321
I choose my own lord too.

04:24.411 --> 04:25.611
My lord

04:25.701 --> 04:28.871
must be the type of man that makes me want
to serve him.

04:31.291 --> 04:32.621
Just kidding.

04:34.501 --> 04:36.671
I'm making a gamble, Bjorn.

04:36.751 --> 04:38.211
If we get lucky,

04:38.291 --> 04:41.421
that prince might completely change.

04:41.511 --> 04:43.591
What are you going to do if you don't get lucky?

04:44.171 --> 04:48.351
He might
get depressed and never recover.

04:48.971 --> 04:51.061
If that happens, I'll abandon him.

04:51.641 --> 04:53.931
He wouldn't deserve to be my lord.

05:02.691 --> 05:04.951
How's it going? Is he going to crack?

05:05.321 --> 05:07.491
He pisses me off.

05:07.571 --> 05:09.451
He won't even scream.

05:09.911 --> 05:12.041
He thinks he's a martyr.

05:12.121 --> 05:15.161
This is why I hate Christians.

05:15.541 --> 05:18.081
You didn't kick him hard enough.

05:18.171 --> 05:19.751
I'll show you how to do it.

05:20.791 --> 05:22.631
This is how you kick!

05:24.881 --> 05:26.051
Like this!

05:27.051 --> 05:28.261
Good job.

05:28.341 --> 05:29.801
You're bad at kicking too.

05:29.891 --> 05:31.061
Kick him in the jaw.

05:31.141 --> 05:33.101
Wait! It's my turn next!

05:33.181 --> 05:34.141
Stop!

05:34.271 --> 05:35.601
Come on!

05:35.681 --> 05:38.191
Don't overdo it, you guys!

05:38.601 --> 05:41.151
If you kill him, we can't get him to talk!

05:42.151 --> 05:45.031
Go ahead and kill me.

05:45.741 --> 05:48.281
The Lord sees everything.

05:48.361 --> 05:52.081
He's seen all the evil things you Danes have done.

05:53.411 --> 05:54.951
He still has some fight left in him.

05:56.751 --> 05:58.121
Do you have any shears?

05:58.211 --> 05:59.631
Go find them.

05:59.711 --> 06:01.291
What?

06:01.381 --> 06:02.711
Shears, right?

06:05.551 --> 06:07.171
Well, then.

06:07.261 --> 06:09.641
I'll say it again, English captain.

06:11.471 --> 06:13.471
There are three things I want to know.

06:13.561 --> 06:15.431
How many reinforcements do they have?

06:15.521 --> 06:18.441
And how long until they get here?

06:19.351 --> 06:22.941
Lastly, how did they find out we're here?

06:23.481 --> 06:25.481
If you tell me, I'll let you live.

06:26.491 --> 06:29.241
You beasts!

06:30.701 --> 06:31.871
You bastards.

06:31.951 --> 06:33.831
You shall be punished.

06:33.991 --> 06:36.451
A death befitting of you bastards

06:36.541 --> 06:38.411
awaits you...

06:41.331 --> 06:44.961
Hey. Will these shears work?

06:45.921 --> 06:46.761
Yeah.

06:50.091 --> 06:51.511
Captain.

06:52.221 --> 06:55.351
Your fingernails are long.

06:56.061 --> 06:57.521
Long fingernails are dirty.

06:57.601 --> 06:59.311
You should cut them.

07:04.061 --> 07:05.691
Oh, sorry!

07:05.771 --> 07:07.151
I cut too deep.

07:08.401 --> 07:09.401
Hold him down.

07:10.951 --> 07:12.741
There are three things I want to know.

07:12.821 --> 07:14.451
I'll skip the rest.

07:18.121 --> 07:20.621
Oh, I cut too deep again!

07:20.711 --> 07:22.711
I did it twice!

07:23.881 --> 07:26.131
That's so nasty.

07:26.211 --> 07:28.381
What's he holding out for?

07:28.761 --> 07:32.301
Go to hell, you Danes!

07:32.381 --> 07:33.431
You bastards!

07:33.551 --> 07:36.641
If you bastards hadn't come...

07:37.011 --> 07:39.771
You bastards burned down my village!

07:39.851 --> 07:43.811
You tortured my wife and daughter and killed them!

07:43.901 --> 07:45.191
You beasts!

07:45.271 --> 07:49.151
This is our land! Leave!

07:50.861 --> 07:52.201
I see.

07:52.281 --> 07:54.411
We're beasts?

07:56.451 --> 07:57.781
You guys are ignorant.

07:57.871 --> 08:00.121
Let me teach you some history.

08:00.661 --> 08:02.371
You should thank me for sharing this,

08:02.461 --> 08:03.461
you Saxon.

08:04.291 --> 08:07.881
Or is it the Anglos who live in this area?

08:07.961 --> 08:10.421
Well, they're the same thing.

08:10.511 --> 08:12.261
This land

08:12.341 --> 08:14.591
didn't belong to you originally.

08:16.141 --> 08:18.641
The first inhabitants were the Celts.

08:18.721 --> 08:21.811
They lived in the forests and worshiped the spirits.

08:21.891 --> 08:24.481
They were the ancestors of the people
who live in Wales now.

08:25.771 --> 08:28.901
Then one day, the Romans came.

08:28.981 --> 08:30.941
They were the rulers,

08:31.031 --> 08:33.241
but they lived on this land alongside the Celts

08:33.321 --> 08:36.281
and gave them their knowledge, technology and culture.

08:37.741 --> 08:39.201
The Romans left,

08:39.281 --> 08:43.211
and then you Anglos and Saxons arrived.

08:43.291 --> 08:45.291
It happened 500 years ago.

08:46.331 --> 08:50.461
You didn't give anything to the Celts.

08:50.711 --> 08:51.801
Instead,

08:52.131 --> 08:54.551
you drove out the Celts from these fertile plains

08:54.631 --> 08:57.301
and forced them to live in the wastelands.

08:57.391 --> 08:58.431
You're lying!

08:58.641 --> 09:00.601
I'm not lying.

09:00.811 --> 09:02.851
If the Danes are beasts,

09:02.931 --> 09:06.691
then you Anglo-Saxons are beasts too.

09:07.731 --> 09:10.611
You stole these lands using violence.

09:10.691 --> 09:14.951
We Danes are going to steal these lands
from you using even greater violence.

09:15.951 --> 09:17.911
You have no objections to that, right?

09:19.281 --> 09:20.621
Shut up!

09:20.701 --> 09:24.581
I don't believe you, you savages!

09:26.711 --> 09:30.171
Teachers hate kids that don't listen.

09:32.341 --> 09:33.511
What?

09:33.591 --> 09:35.091
Captain.

09:35.551 --> 09:39.341
Now that I've got a good look at your face...

09:40.221 --> 09:42.261
Your nose is long.

09:45.481 --> 09:46.811
Askeladd!

09:53.321 --> 09:54.781
How many are there, Ear?

09:54.861 --> 09:56.991
I'm not sure. But there's a lot.

09:57.071 --> 09:58.611
They're coming from the south!

09:58.861 --> 10:00.121
Enemy reinforcements?

10:00.201 --> 10:01.911
In the middle of the night?

10:03.331 --> 10:06.461
The English are attacking at night? Impressive.

10:08.961 --> 10:10.041
They're here!

10:11.341 --> 10:14.421
It's too late! You bastards are going to die!

10:14.841 --> 10:18.301
I can't wait to see you Danes eat each other alive!

10:18.381 --> 10:20.641
-Danes?
-I'll tell you what's happening.

10:20.721 --> 10:22.801
Thorkell's coming!

10:22.891 --> 10:24.721
Not a bad match, right?

10:25.101 --> 10:26.351
It's Thorkell!

10:26.431 --> 10:29.141
Did he say Thorkell? What are we going to do?

10:29.311 --> 10:30.981
Hey.

10:31.061 --> 10:32.561
Did he say Thorkell?

10:32.651 --> 10:35.321
Who knows? I thought that's what he said.

10:35.571 --> 10:37.821
If it's true, we're in trouble.

10:38.901 --> 10:40.821
Thorkell?

10:40.911 --> 10:42.321
Did you say Thorkell?

10:42.411 --> 10:43.331
No way!

10:43.411 --> 10:44.871
Really?

10:46.501 --> 10:48.541
Thorkell's coming!

10:55.131 --> 10:56.631
Is that the village?

10:56.711 --> 10:58.511
That's what it looks like.

10:58.971 --> 11:01.471
All right! We're going to surround them!

11:01.551 --> 11:04.051
Vali and Ingolf's units, take the left!

11:04.141 --> 11:05.681
Oddr, take the right!

11:05.761 --> 11:07.601
I'm going to take the middle.

11:08.061 --> 11:10.021
Kill anyone you see!

11:10.101 --> 11:12.061
But don't kill the prince.

11:12.151 --> 11:15.021
And there should be a kid with a knife.

11:16.691 --> 11:18.491
Don't kill him either.

11:21.571 --> 11:23.911
He's my playmate.

11:24.701 --> 11:26.451
Thorkell's coming!

11:26.541 --> 11:29.041
Let me go, you buffoon!

11:29.121 --> 11:31.001
Are you going to disobey my orders?

11:32.081 --> 11:34.501
I can't leave Ragnar behind!

11:34.581 --> 11:37.961
I'm not going without Ragnar!

11:38.591 --> 11:40.551
Forget about it, Your Highness.

11:40.841 --> 11:44.851
We only have three sleds.
We don't have room for a corpse.

11:44.931 --> 11:46.931
Then let's hold a funeral for him.

11:47.011 --> 11:49.851
Pay your respects to the death of a warrior!
This is an order!

11:49.931 --> 11:52.691
We don't have enough time for that either.

11:53.731 --> 11:54.981
You bastard!

11:58.021 --> 12:01.491
No! I'm not going!

12:01.571 --> 12:03.991
Ragnar! Ragnar--

12:14.791 --> 12:19.251
Ragnar is dead. He won't come even if you call for him.

12:24.761 --> 12:27.051
You bastard...

12:29.471 --> 12:30.471
Askeladd!

12:31.141 --> 12:34.231
They're deserters. They were planning to join Thorkell.

12:36.611 --> 12:38.651
They were hiding in the straw.

12:44.781 --> 12:47.451
Ragnar was right!

12:47.531 --> 12:49.871
Luck's not on your side right now.

12:50.911 --> 12:52.751
We're not the only ones.

12:52.831 --> 12:55.961
Everyone knows we're in trouble.

12:56.041 --> 12:59.881
We're in big trouble this time. You're...

13:00.881 --> 13:03.011
Thorkell has you by the tail.

13:10.681 --> 13:12.351
Go ahead.

13:12.851 --> 13:16.651
Listen, men. Follow whichever leader you want.

13:17.521 --> 13:20.821
If you're going to leave, then leave!
I won't blame you.

13:20.901 --> 13:22.941
If you're going to come with me,

13:23.901 --> 13:25.151
then march!

13:27.741 --> 13:30.661
We're going to march until we lose Thorkell!

13:32.081 --> 13:35.331
Walk while you eat, and walk while you sleep!

13:36.251 --> 13:37.711
Listen, men!

13:37.791 --> 13:40.131
If you can't keep up, then you're dead.

14:12.281 --> 14:13.491
Wait, Thorkell!

14:13.581 --> 14:16.501
We're not like Askeladd.

14:16.581 --> 14:19.001
We want to join you--

14:27.971 --> 14:30.721
So, your leader's name is Askeladd?

14:34.681 --> 14:36.891
Oh, what a nice sword.

14:36.981 --> 14:40.311
-It's mine now!
-Oh, nice.

14:40.401 --> 14:43.361
The fact that some of their men deserted

14:43.441 --> 14:46.991
means they must be really worried.

14:47.071 --> 14:48.901
Poor things.

14:48.991 --> 14:51.361
You should've just let them join us.

14:51.451 --> 14:54.331
It's okay. They're worthless.

14:54.411 --> 14:58.661
I don't need cowards who surrender
without putting up a fight.

15:01.831 --> 15:05.671
Men, to the east! We're going to chase down the prince!

15:05.751 --> 15:07.841
Give it everything you got!

15:07.921 --> 15:09.721
Yeah!

15:15.181 --> 15:17.431
The right! You're too far to the right!

15:17.521 --> 15:19.101
Move it back.

15:19.181 --> 15:21.691
No! I meant my right.

15:22.811 --> 15:25.021
JANUARY 1014 AD
UPPER SEVERN RIVER, EARLDOM OF MERCIA

15:25.111 --> 15:27.651
-That's right. Keep going. Go slow.
-Heave ho!

15:27.731 --> 15:28.821
Hurry up!

15:28.901 --> 15:30.571
You're holding us up back here!

15:34.741 --> 15:37.541
Torgrim. Atli. Come with me.

15:37.621 --> 15:38.751
-Okay.
-Okay.

15:39.871 --> 15:42.961
Destroy this bridge. You guys take the lead.

15:43.041 --> 15:44.921
-Hurry.
-Okay.

15:45.341 --> 15:47.381
We're going to take the bridge apart.

15:47.461 --> 15:49.591
Pitch in if you have an ax!

15:50.381 --> 15:52.091
I'm so tired.

15:52.181 --> 15:54.471
Is Thorkell nearby, Ear?

15:54.551 --> 15:56.471
They're being too loud. I'm not sure.

15:56.551 --> 15:59.061
We might have enough time to destroy the bridge.

16:10.991 --> 16:13.491
Hey! Hold on! You, there, priest!

16:13.571 --> 16:16.031
What are you doing?

16:16.121 --> 16:18.161
Do you have any booze?

16:18.241 --> 16:21.001
Even if I did, I wouldn't give you any.

16:21.081 --> 16:23.421
We don't even have enough for ourselves.

16:23.501 --> 16:25.421
I don't have any booze for you.

16:25.501 --> 16:29.001
Can't you tell we're in a tight spot right now, priest?

16:45.981 --> 16:48.441
The water's really cold.

16:48.521 --> 16:51.481
Hey! This river's pretty shallow.

16:52.491 --> 16:54.611
They'll be able to cross it on foot!

16:54.701 --> 16:56.531
What's the point of destroying the bridge?

16:57.991 --> 17:01.161
But we can't just leave it here.

17:01.241 --> 17:03.461
Maybe it'll piss them off at least.

17:05.921 --> 17:10.751
Looks like Askeladd ran out
of those bright ideas of his.

17:19.511 --> 17:21.141
Bjorn! Thorfinn!

17:29.401 --> 17:31.191
-What's wrong?
-Come over here.

17:32.281 --> 17:33.191
What's going on?

17:35.201 --> 17:38.661
Bjorn. Move the prince over to this carriage here.

17:38.741 --> 17:40.491
You be the driver.

17:40.581 --> 17:44.081
Thorfinn, you ride with the prince. Be on standby.

17:44.161 --> 17:45.661
What?

17:48.171 --> 17:49.081
Hey!

17:50.171 --> 17:51.001
Askeladd!

17:52.001 --> 17:52.841
Are you serious?

17:55.341 --> 17:56.841
It's my special talent.

17:58.051 --> 18:00.091
I can tell what a man is like

18:00.181 --> 18:02.601
just by looking at his face.

18:03.221 --> 18:06.141
Whether he's an important man, or a nobody.
Smart, or dumb.

18:06.851 --> 18:11.521
I can tell that
there are some traitors among the loyal.

18:13.191 --> 18:14.611
What?

18:15.111 --> 18:16.651
Take the prince? Are you crazy?

18:16.741 --> 18:18.611
Idiot! Don't say it so loudly!

18:19.241 --> 18:20.411
Atli.

18:20.491 --> 18:23.081
This army is done for already.

18:23.161 --> 18:26.791
Let's join Thorkell's army
and give him the prince as a gift.

18:26.871 --> 18:29.871
More than half of the other men are already on our side.

18:30.581 --> 18:33.041
We'll be able to convince the other half easily.

18:34.501 --> 18:35.961
You're going to betray him?

18:37.721 --> 18:39.381
Betray Askeladd?

18:39.931 --> 18:43.561
Don't call it a betrayal, Atli.

18:43.641 --> 18:46.391
He's a good leader. He's done a good job.

18:47.391 --> 18:50.561
That's why we're going to make him
take responsibility as the leader.

18:50.651 --> 18:53.731
We'll be fine! We'll be able to escape!

18:53.821 --> 18:55.981
We've always been able to escape, right?

18:56.071 --> 18:58.111
Well, up until now.

18:58.191 --> 19:00.361
But what about recently?

19:00.451 --> 19:03.201
He's made the wrong call, one after the other.

19:03.281 --> 19:05.031
He's run out of luck.

19:05.121 --> 19:07.911
And Thorkell found us,
even though we thought he was beat.

19:10.251 --> 19:12.081
Don't look at me like that.

19:13.081 --> 19:16.591
Well, you're right. He's a good leader.

19:17.461 --> 19:21.011
Then why did he mess with Thorkell?

19:21.091 --> 19:22.431
Brother...

19:22.511 --> 19:24.221
I'm not happy about this either.

19:25.221 --> 19:26.891
But we can't help it.

19:27.521 --> 19:29.891
Askeladd made a bet, and he lost.

19:30.811 --> 19:31.981
That's all.

19:43.201 --> 19:44.911
Good job.

19:45.531 --> 19:49.161
They're going to have a hard time getting their
sleds and cargo across.

19:49.251 --> 19:51.501
What if they abandon their cargo and keep chasing us?

19:51.581 --> 19:55.341
Then they're going to lose time finding food.

19:55.421 --> 19:57.961
They won't be able to follow us very far without eating.

19:58.961 --> 20:01.721
All right! Resume the march!

20:10.021 --> 20:10.851
They're here!

20:18.691 --> 20:20.401
Oh, I saw a flash!

20:41.091 --> 20:44.341
I...

20:44.431 --> 20:46.091
found you!

20:54.641 --> 20:56.651
-Unbelievable!
-No way...

20:56.731 --> 20:59.481
-A spear?
-Three of them? That's impossible!

20:59.571 --> 21:00.901
No! There were four of them!

21:00.981 --> 21:02.741
-This is bad.
-Damn! This is bad!

21:02.821 --> 21:04.321
-This is really bad!
-All right!

21:05.071 --> 21:07.701
Calm down, men!

21:07.781 --> 21:09.371
He's still far away.

21:09.451 --> 21:12.951
And we destroyed the bridge.
Forget about that spear just now.

21:13.041 --> 21:14.661
Bridge?

21:14.751 --> 21:16.501
What about the bridge?

21:16.581 --> 21:19.541
They'll be able to cross that river on foot!

21:19.631 --> 21:21.551
Destroying the bridge was useless!

21:21.631 --> 21:23.131
Is that what you think?

21:23.211 --> 21:25.721
If that's what you think,
then we're leaving right now.

21:25.801 --> 21:27.891
Every minute is precious.

21:29.641 --> 21:31.431
Not again!

21:31.511 --> 21:33.851
You keep saying march, march, march!

21:33.931 --> 21:35.941
Don't you know any other words?

21:36.021 --> 21:37.441
You!

21:40.021 --> 21:41.821
We can't win against Thorkell.

21:42.861 --> 21:45.111
Just bear with it for one more day.

21:45.191 --> 21:47.451
Destroying the bridge will start to pay off then.

21:49.241 --> 21:51.831
They can only march as fast as they can
carry their cargo.

21:51.911 --> 21:55.081
They're going to have trouble getting their cargo across.

21:55.161 --> 21:59.081
If they leave their cargo behind to chase us,
they won't be able to replenish supplies.

21:59.171 --> 22:02.171
They'll only be able to march for one day like that.

22:02.251 --> 22:03.841
Understand, men?

22:04.511 --> 22:06.471
If you understand, start marching!

22:06.761 --> 22:10.091
There's no guarantee we'll be able
to survive one more day!

22:16.431 --> 22:19.901
Oh, really? Then this is where we say goodbye.

22:19.981 --> 22:22.071
I'm in a hurry. Excuse me.
